  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-08T00:00:00Z",
      "text": "Mexican Navy personnel working with intelligence from the National Intelligence Center and the U.S. DEA, arrest Rafael Álvarez Ayala, the alleged leader of the Jalisco New Generation Cartel cell \"Los Rs\", in Zapopan…",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-08:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-08T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "In 1940, under president Lázaro Cárdenas and the direction of Mexican psychiatrist Leopoldo Salazar Viniegra, Mexico legalized all drugs…",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384243123:19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-08T00:00:16Z",
      "text": "The Mexican drug war is an ongoing asymmetric armed conflict between the Mexican government and various drug trafficking syndicates.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384243123:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-08T00:00:24Z",
      "text": "On the map: National Intelligence Centre, Mexico, where the reports place it.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-08:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-08T00:00:32Z",
      "text": "The article lists two sides: Mexico, Armed Forces, *; Mexican cartels:, Sinaloa Cartel, CJNG.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1384243123:side-1",
        "wiki:box:1384243123:side-2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-08T00:00:40Z",
      "text": "Wikipedia lists it as ongoing.",
